Question 1 :    Why is Binary Search faster than Linear Search?
                I'm not asking for the complexity.
                I'm asking for the reason.

  Think carefully.

=====================================================================================================================
Linear Search
                  2
                  5
                  8
                  10
                  13
                  18
                  21
                  30

        Worst case:      Visit  every element
        Time: O(n)

=====================================================================================================================
Binary Search  :     Look at the middle.
                      2
                      5
                      8
                      10
                      13
                      18
                      21
                      30
                                ^

            Suppose    middle = 13
            Found. Done.

          But suppose the target is  21
          
          Middle  : 13
          
          Now ask: Is   21 > 13 ?
          Yes.

        Can we safely ignore
                      2                      
                      5                      
                      8                      
                      10                      
                      13

                    ?                    
                    Yes.                    
                    Why?  :  Because the array is sorted.
                    
                    Every element on the left is <= 13
                    None of them can possibly be:   21
                    
                    So we've eliminated half the search space.
                    
              *****  This is the key idea.
=====================================================================================================================
What is Search Space?

            This is one of the most important interview concepts.
            
          Initially Search Space :    [2 5 8 10 13 18 21 30]

          After one comparison :    [18 21 30]
        
          After another :          [21]

  Each comparison cuts the search space approximately in half.
  
  Binary Search is not about the middle element.
  
  It is about reducing the search space.

